<BaseLayout title="Lab Tales 2023 — Upasana Sridhar" description="Reflections from the Lab Tales workshop at Princeton.">
  <article class="container section article-page">
    <p class="article-back"><a href={`${base}/writing`}>← Writing</a></p>
    <h1 class="section-heading">Lab Tales 2023</h1>
    <p class="post-date article-date">July 31, 2023</p>
    <p class="tag-list article-tags"><span class="tag">Research life</span></p>

    <p>I’m so glad I attended the Lab Tales workshop at Princeton! Thank you to the organizers, Daniel Cohen, Annetta Black, and the Council on Science and Technology at Princeton.</p>
    <p>This was the first time they opened it to external attendees and, luckily, Professor Tom Zajdel sent out an email about it.</p>
    <p>Before I get to gushing about the workshop, I want to talk about how it was the perfect atmosphere in which to visit Princeton. The <em>Oppenheimer</em> movie had just come out. I hadn’t seen it yet, and roaming around the Princeton campus felt like priming myself for Easter eggs in the movie. The workshop also used Oppenheimer as a backdrop for some of its motivation.</p>
    <p>I don’t want to spoil what the workshop is like for future attendees, so this post documents some of the work that came out of attending.</p>

    <h2>An accessible description of what I work on</h2>
    <p>Simple Writer wouldn’t let me use jargon such as “program” or “multiple,” so this was a little difficult. But I think the exercise was useful for distilling the work to its fundamentals. Personally, it made the process of writing less daunting.</p>
    <figure class="simple-writer">
      <a href={`${base}/writing/SimpleWriter.png`} aria-label="View the Simple Writer exercise at full size">
        <img src={`${base}/writing/SimpleWriter.png`} width="2048" height="987" loading="lazy" alt="Simple Writer exercise comparing computers to kitchens: just as cooking improves with practice, writing fast code improves with experience. My research finds reusable steps and puts them together into a book." />
      </a>
      <figcaption>My research, explained using Simple Writer. Select the image to view it at full size.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>Without any restrictions, here’s what I work on in simple language:</p>
    <blockquote>High-performance computing is often gate-kept as an “art” that you have to be a natural at. But I strongly believe that it is a craft to be honed. There are certain techniques that you have in your arsenal, and you apply them as appropriate. My work is to identify general techniques and describe recipes for their application.</blockquote>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

